From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:26:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: reset: macsmc-reboot: declare the resume
 exception reader early

reboot_prepare clears the early resume exception record, but the
function that reads and clears it is defined further down, so the
driver does not build as a module:

  error: call to undeclared function 'macsmc_reboot_resume_exception'

Declare it before its first use.

Fixes: a1c7b72f7a ("power: reset: macsmc-reboot: print an early resume exception record")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/power/reset/macsmc-reboot.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/macsmc-reboot.c b/drivers/power/reset/macsmc-reboot.c
index 1f9d1dd1da..8a9b855794 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/macsmc-reboot.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/macsmc-reboot.c
@@ -156,6 +156,8 @@ static int macsmc_restart(struct sys_off_data *data)
 	return NOTIFY_OK;
 }
 
+static void macsmc_reboot_resume_exception(struct macsmc_reboot *reboot, bool print);
+
 static int macsmc_reboot_notify(struct notifier_block *this, unsigned long action, void *data)
 {
 	struct macsmc_reboot *reboot = container_of(this, struct macsmc_reboot, reboot_notify);
-- 
2.43.0

